aken seriously when you started the  reviews were not always so nice totally  i remember i read one that said your  your clothes were silly yeah or like or  too  too much was that a specific thing that  they were needling it was like they  couldn't figure it out his critics also  couldn't figure out why an aspiring  serious designer would want to make  cheaper collections for more affordable  brands did you shop at payless as a kid  i did of course so growing up i didn't  want to say no to that also because like  that's where i grew up like my mom is a  teacher like that we shopped there  my mom shopped at lane bryant i did a  collection for lane bryant and i also  was very excited i was never one to  alienate a customer you never know  someone can shop at payless one day  but you never know where they're  shopping 10 years later did you ever  have a moment of  like panic like maybe this isn't going  to work or or maybe that every day i  still have it it's great  dozens of successful collaborations and  more than a decade of runway shows later  so this is our world  i would like to live here please yes  live here please this is incredible but  if you live here you have to start  sewing  that's not going to go well for you  siriano has mastered the tool of his  tray i love the color of this dress i  actually have no idea where this woman's  going and she's fabulous and i'm like  where are you going like oh you don't  know where she's going in this dress  she just bought this dress and i swear i  hope she wears it to the grocery store  all these dresses are custom made to  order i'm pretty much in the whole  process starting with a sketch then  brought to life  stitch by meticulous stitch  one of the first things i noticed when i  walked in is also your mannequin bodies  are different sizes yeah every single  mannequin is a different size you know  because everybody's body is different  siriano's consistent willingness to  dress anybody and anybody has helped  earn him a stable of loyal celebrity  clients like lizzo lady gaga laverne cox  and leslie jones and i was like we're  gonna make you look incredible and she  looked like she felt oh my god we were  like this is your pretty woman moment  after jones tweeted that she couldn't  get a fancy designer to work with her  siriano replied with what else a raised  hand emoji you're coming out you're  going to wear this red gown you're also  going to show the world that like yes  you're tall and curvy but you also have  an amazing body she really does that  gown and dozens of others are now part  of an exhibit people are people on  display in atlanta i think it's  important for like other people to feel  represented and like celebrities on  screen oh my god that's someone with my  body type on screen and then they can  feel more comfortable with who they are  kelly dyer brought her daughter ruby i  try to teach my girls that you have your  body and you should be proud of it and  you can wear what you want and now i'm  getting emotional  do you have a favorite dress  a favorite dress no  impossible now i have had favorite like  moments um  like billy porter's oscar moment i think  was probably one of my favorite moments  in my career just because of what it  meant what did it mean i just think it  was  the ultimate  showcase of  what clothes can do to transform  someone's opinion about the world  because in syriano's world you can wear  whatever you want almost anywhere we  should be able to  walk and talk and be who we want to be  we're not carrying cancer here like it's  a dress calm down  so long as it makes you feel great  for cbs morning's christina raffini new  york that part of it the feeling great  as somebody who grew up as a kid that  was not a traditional size and didn't  have options when you find clothes that  make you feel the way you want to feel  that's right and make you see yourself  in a different way that's everything so  what he does for everyone of all sizes  completely hands down love it there  should be more designers that approach  it from that perspective that body  positivity for everybody should  represent  every woman every man yeah i mean he  says we're not curing cancer but you  could wear the dress to a cancer benefit  and steal the show on the red carpet as  you guys said that yellow dress that's  gayle's yellow we got we got to get that  dress for games christina rafini should  have had a dress made for herself in the  name of journalism in the name of yes  this time charge it to cbs otherwise  great story but missed opportunities

